From 6b4d9fa67adb2aac5bb987340b409c6349a6b4c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 16:06:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] quote REALITY short-id in clash output; harden sid parsing;
 fix sing-box tls output

- Clash/ClashR output now force-quotes short-id values. YAML 1.1 parsers
  (go-yaml used by Clash Verge/Mihomo) previously reinterpreted values
  like 72696e32 as float 7.2696e36, corrupting the sid during the
  clash-verge-check.yaml round-trip and causing 'invalid REALITY short ID'.
- Parser drops invalid (odd-length/non-hex/oversized) short IDs with a
  warning instead of emitting configs that fail whole-subscription checks.
- Clash generator emits reality-opts whenever public-key exists, so nodes
  with an omitted short-id keep their reality settings.
- Sing-box: merge tls.server_name/insecure into the existing tls object
  instead of emitting a duplicate tls key that overwrote reality/utls.
- Sing-box AnyTLS: fix fingerprint being written as insecure=true.

